# Cat Jam Free — negative findings by GPT 5.6 Sol

- Source: OpenCode (`opencode/cat-jam-free`)
- Date: 2026-10-17 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Cat Jam Free
- **Short description:** A short-lived, undisclosed OpenCode free-tier reasoning route for coding and agentic workflows. The project tracks it under `cat-jam`; no distinct non-free `cat-jam` route was found.
- **Provider / access:** Historical OpenCode OpenAI-compatible endpoint as `opencode/cat-jam-free`. The route appeared in OpenCode's built-in model list and has since been removed ([OpenCode issue snapshot](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/55150), [removal tracker](https://github.com/trefeon/pi-freeflow/issues/77)).
- **Release / knowledge:** Archived catalog metadata lists release 2026-10-12; no knowledge cutoff was published ([archived models.dev record](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anomalyco/models.dev/d8a3fdfb7206e6b1b0aac70df3819dc4970b071b/providers/opencode/models/cat-jam-free.toml)).
- **IDs:** `opencode/cat-jam-free`; the earlier `catjam` catalog ID was explicitly renamed to `cat-jam-free` on 2026-10-13 ([models.dev rename commit](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/0d48ea55e5dd13326670e0401b67660f9aab5e61)).
- **Context window:** Archived metadata lists 1,048,576 total tokens and 131,072 maximum output. The context value was raised from 262,144 on 2026-10-15, but no retrieval-at-length result was published ([archived models.dev record](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anomalyco/models.dev/d8a3fdfb7206e6b1b0aac70df3819dc4970b071b/providers/opencode/models/cat-jam-free.toml), [context update](https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/9c040469a99e1a7bb67d08ed37e0df339ea92fb4)).
- **Modalities:** Text input and text output; reasoning effort controls, tool calling, and structured output were advertised. No image, audio, video, or non-text output support was listed ([archived models.dev record](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anomalyco/models.dev/d8a3fdfb7206e6b1b0aac70df3819dc4970b071b/providers/opencode/models/cat-jam-free.toml)).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-17):** The route was free while active. Independent tracking places its free window at 2026-10-13 through 2026-10-16 ([free-model tracker](https://github.com/TobiasBak/dotfiles/issues/15)).
- **Architecture:** Closed weights; developer, parameter count, architecture, license, and underlying model identity were not disclosed.

